Creating a List within a DataQueue or DataStack
Creating a List within a DataQueue or DataStack
To create a sublist or a subtable in objects of type DataQueue or DataStack:
• Add the sublist to a cell within the object, compare Creating Lists within Lists and Tables.
• Insert a list object from the Class Library into your simulation model: Drag that object to the active cell
of the DataQueue/DataStack and drop it there. This inserts the path to and the name of the list or table
into the active cell. Compare Insert a List into a DataTable from a Frame.
• Assign a DataList to a DataQueue or a DataStack in a Method.
Creating a List within a DataQueue or DataStack
11-3946 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Assign a DataList to a DataQueue or a DataStack in a Method
Within a Method you can declare a local variable of data type Stack, Queue, List, and Table.
After you created a list of these types, you can assign it to cells in a queue or stack. Initially, all of the cells
of the local variable are void.
Only when Plant Simulation creates the list, by executing the method create [SimTalk] - local list, it will
actually create it and enter a pointer to this new list into the DataList. The graphic below illustrates this.
Syntax
<Local-variable>.create
Now you can enter data. Our list will then look like this:
Example
var l: list[string]
l.create
l.insert(1,"Hello") 
You can then insert this list into another list, as illustrated below (see also Common Format [check box]).
