Assign a List to a DataList in a Method
Within a Method you can assign a local variable of data type Stack, Queue, List, and Table. After you
created a list of these types, you can assign it to cells in a list. Initially, all of the cells of the local variable
are void.
Only when Plant Simulation creates the list, by executing the method create [SimTalk] - local list, it will
actually create it and enter a pointer to this new list into the DataList.
Syntax
<Local-variable>.create
Now, you can enter values.
Example
var s: stack[string]
s.create
s.insert("Hello")
You can then insert this list into another list, as illustrated below (see also Common Format [check box]).
See also
createNestedList [SimTalk] - DataQueue
createNestedList [SimTalk] - DataList
createNestedList [SimTalk] - DataTable
