Creating a List within a DataTable
Creating a List within a DataTable
To create a list or table in an object of type DataTable.
• Add the sublist to a cell within the object, compare Creating Lists within Lists and Tables.
• Insert a List into a DataTable from a Frame, drag that object to the active cell of the DataTable and
drop it there. This inserts the path to and the name of the list or table into the active cell.
• Assign a List to a DataTable in a Method.
Creating a List within a DataTable
11-3952 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Insert a List into a DataTable from a Frame
When you insert a DataTable from the Class Library into your simulation model, it will be empty as it is
unknown at this time how many columns and rows it will contain.
Only when Plant Simulation creates the DataTable, by running the method createNestedList, it will
actually create it and enter a pointer to this new list into the DataTable.
Syntax
<Path>.createNestedList(index1,index2)
The expression Path designates the name of the DataTable in which Plant Simulation creates the subtable
designated by the parameter [index1,index2].
The method create can access every position. If you create a list in an entry that already contains an entry,
Plant Simulation, overwrites the existing entry.
Let us say we have a DataTable some of whose cells contain other DataTables:
Example
MyDataTable.createNestedList(2,1) // creates the first entry
MyDataTable[2,1][1,1] := "Hello"  // DataTable in DataTable
The method DataTable[2,1] returns the table occupying the first cell on the table. Accessing the index at
the coordinates [1,1] and using an assignment you now may enter a string into the table, as illustrated
below.
